From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:28:34 +0200
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: cbm: drop the unused qen_pos in
 counter_mode_set

cbm_counter_mode_set() loads qen_pos with the bit position of the
counter-enable field and never reads it again: QEN is only ever cleared
and set, which qen_mask alone does. Its sibling msel_pos is genuinely
read, twice -- MSEL carries a value rather than a state, so extracting
the current mode and inserting the new one both need the shift. Both
fields are one bit wide (BIT(4) and BIT(5) in cbm_regs.h); it is what
the code does with them, not their width, that decides whether the
position is needed.

W=1 flags the store as -Wunused-but-set-variable, which CONFIG_WERROR
turns into a build failure. Remove the variable and the two assignments;
EQM_QEN_POS and DQM_QEN_POS stay in cbm_regs.h next to the masks they
describe.

No functional change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_basic.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_basic.c
index 8192c4cd8158..19aa84b53fb4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_basic.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_basic.c
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ int cbm_counter_mode_set(int idx, int mode)
 {
 	u32 val;
 	u32 curr_mode;
-	u32 qen_mask, qen_pos, msel_mask, msel_pos;
+	u32 qen_mask, msel_mask, msel_pos;
 
 	if (!g_cbm_eqm_base || !g_cbm_dqm_base) {
 		pr_warn_once("cbm: counter_mode_set(idx=%d) before CBM probe, skipping\n",
@@ -78,7 +78,6 @@ int cbm_counter_mode_set(int idx, int mode)
 	switch (idx) {
 	case 0:
 		qen_mask  = EQM_QEN_MASK;
-		qen_pos   = EQM_QEN_POS;
 		msel_mask = EQM_MSEL_MASK;
 		msel_pos  = EQM_MSEL_POS;
 		val = cbm_eqm_r32(CBM_EQM_CTRL);
@@ -98,7 +97,6 @@ int cbm_counter_mode_set(int idx, int mode)
 
 	case 1:
 		qen_mask  = DQM_QEN_MASK;
-		qen_pos   = DQM_QEN_POS;
 		msel_mask = DQM_MSEL_MASK;
 		msel_pos  = DQM_MSEL_POS;
 		val = cbm_dqm_r32(CBM_DQM_CTRL);
